Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, is pleased to submit a tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval. Our proposed solution leverages our expertise in AI/ML capabilities, particularly large language models like Mistral 7B and CamemBERT, and RAG frameworks like LangChain, to provide assistance with information consultation, drafting, file instruction, and collaboration. We ensure strict compliance with GDPR, EU AI Act, and other regulatory requirements through robust security controls, data protection measures, and transparent AI decision-making processes. Our proposal aligns with the City's digital transformation strategy, aiming to improve efficiency and service quality while respecting budgetary constraints and environmental considerations.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an artificial intelligence solution to enhance municipal agents' daily tasks, including information search, drafting, file instruction, and collaboration. The solution must integrate into existing systems, ensure high availability (99.9%), respond within 2 seconds, and adhere to strict GDPR compliance, explicability, and transparency requirements. The project's total budget is 3 million euros over 4 years, with an emphasis on cost optimization without compromising quality.

# Proposed Solution
To meet the City's requirements, we propose a solution that utilizes our existing stack and expertise. We will deploy on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, specifically using OVHcloud or Scaleway as our cloud provider, ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory demands. Our API integration layer will connect with required software systems, including civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories, leveraging experience with GED systems like Alfresco and Maarch Courrier.

For AI capabilities, we will utilize Mistral 7B and CamemBERT models, fine-tuned for the client's specific use cases, along with LangChain RAG frameworks to facilitate access to up-to-date information. To optimize performance, we will implement quantisation methods like INT8 or INT4. Our solution ensures explicability and transparency through output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation.

The budget for this project is aligned with the client's expectations, totaling 3 million euros over 4 years. We propose a flexible pricing model that includes a discounted rate for a longer contract commitment and explores alternative delivery models like outcome-based contracting. Our projected annual margin could be around 210,000 euros, considering our target gross margin percentage of 28%. However, we are open to adjusting our pricing strategy to respect municipal budget capacity constraints.

From a legal standpoint, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. operates within the EU, ensuring intra-EU data hosting and processing compliance with GDPR Article 6(1)(e). Our standard contractual clauses will be reviewed and amended as necessary to explicitly address GDPR compliance, explainable AI recommendations, and human validation of automated decisions.

Our security posture includes a strong GDPR compliance framework, anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio, and custom NER models for sensitive data protection. We will conduct thorough security audits and implement enhanced access controls, logging, and monitoring as needed.

To support the City's sustainability goals, we propose eco-friendly solutions through partnerships with green hosting providers OVHcloud and Scaleway, who use 100% renewable energy. Our digital sobriety practices include model quantisation, auto-scaling, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, aiming to reduce energy consumption by approximately 35%.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender are left unaddressed in our proposal.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its consortium partners, is well-positioned to deliver an innovative AI solution that meets the City of Belval's needs for improving municipal agents' efficiency and service quality. Our proposed solution respects all regulatory, security, and environmental requirements while offering a cost-effective approach that aligns with the City's budgetary constraints. We are committed to collaborating closely with the City to ensure the successful deployment and ongoing support of this critical project.
